{"study_accession":"PRJNA1525242","secondary_study_accession":"SRP734502","title":"Transcriptomic profiling of tumor-associated macrophages following CRISPR–Cas9 perturbation of myeloid lectins in a human breast cancer co-culture model","description":"Tumor-associated macrophages (TAMs) integrate multiple signals from the tumor microenvironment, including lectin-mediated recognition of tumor-associated glycans. To investigate the contribution of individual myeloid lectin receptors to tumor-conditioned macrophage states, primary human monocytes from four healthy donors were subjected to CRISPR–Cas9 ribonucleoprotein (RNP)-mediated perturbation of CLEC4E, CLEC6A, CD209, SELL, or SIGLEC9 and subsequently co-cultured with BT474 breast cancer cells for 7 days. Viable CD45-positive macrophages were isolated by fluorescence-activated cell sorting and analyzed by bulk RNA sequencing. The dataset enables paired, donor-matched analysis of target-specific and shared transcriptional responses to myeloid lectin perturbation.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":28,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN63000154","study_accession":"PRJNA1525242","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"HD183 SIGLEC9-targeted TAMs","description":"HD183 SIGLEC9-targeted TAMs","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM10033483","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-09-11","attributes":[["source_name","peripheral blood"],["tissue","peripheral blood"],["cell_type","tumor-associated macrophages"],["crispr condition","SIGLEC9"],["sgrna sequence","GGTAAATCCAGCCATGCGAG"],["donor","HD183"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR40560771","experiment_accession":"SRX35148689","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":0,"base_count":0,"first_public":"2026-09-11","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM10033483: HD183 SIGLEC9-targeted TAMs Homo sapiens RNA-